  "sourceReview": [
    {
      "topic": "Precise fault boundary",
      "finding": "The original prepare response is forwarded only after the independent HANDLE capture. HostWindowsLaunch awaits installOwner before sending Resume. The observer holds the first Resume for attachment A and the one prepared capability before original.handle; no physical Resume or successful result is fabricated."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Loss attribution",
      "finding": "The open promise is observed pending and A is observed nonaborted immediately before the single exclusive marker write. The same captured child exit and abort precede accepting exactly HostClientError transport-closed/unknown. Timeout, not-dispatched, earlier completion, or unrelated error cannot pass."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Recovery and durable history",
      "finding": "Host B attaches only after A exit/abort. Actual hello incarnation belongs to its attachment; Runtime journal incarnation is independently retained. Public read precedes one explicit reconcile; identical original intent replay preserves held/unknown and no new allocation, prepare, Resume, write or peer journal rows."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Native negatives",
      "finding": "Four direct original-port negatives retain stale-A versus successor-B capability checks; numeric PID is refused by the strict public Runtime payload. These do not substitute for original queryable HANDLE identity or ordinary business execution."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Cleanup",
      "finding": "Original CapturedHostClient shutdown and original Main close remain the only owners. Main physical cleanup and HANDLE absence are separate from Host providerCustody unresolved and the persistent held/unknown record. Expected lost callback is separately identified; all other callback/cleanup errors remain observable and block PASS."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Partial evidence",
      "finding": "The normal Gate creates and retains the INCOMPLETE ownerLoss object before its first await and ordinary cases; helper phases mutate that same external-finally receipt. This is not a guarantee for arbitrary synchronous setup failures before the original Gate try or controller hard termination."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Preservation and closure",
      "finding": "All five original files invert exactly. Original ordinary providers and source branch, source A/B resumed predicates, commands, matrices, budgets, artifact paths, and W07/compiler/lint neighbors remain. New helper is process-gate-only; no Desktop roster expansion is needed."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Qualification",
      "finding": "Source-only acceptance does not establish canonical TS/lint, timing inside the original controller120s, Windows x64/ARM runtime behavior, broader W05, W07, same-Main Desktop Retry, P09, Ready, release, or genuine vendor qualification."
    }
  ],
